<o:Entity Id="o103">
<a:ObjectID>8B96AF85-BE06-4205-987F-A5792D84BEDE</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>SALES_AREA</a:Name>
<a:Code>SLS_AR</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1727675606</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>Koyel.Ghatak</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1728887933</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>Koyel.Ghatak</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Generally a single customer record can be extended to multiple Sales Areas to reflect the different business relationships the customer may have with the various businesses within Shell.
 
A Sales Area is made up via the combination of: Sales Organisation,Distribution Channel,Division
A customer can be extended to multiple Sales Areas for doing business with more than one legal Shell entity (OU), more than one Distribution Channel (Class of Sales Accountability) and Division (Class of Product).
Stores the customer master sales area data. assuming you want to see the customer belonging to a particular sales area.

SAP table: KNVV
When a customer is set up in more than one of the following Distribution Channels;-
•	02-Global Commercial Fuels, 
•	08-Global Lubricants and 
•	13-Global Bitumen,
the Divisions:
•	02-Fuels or 
•	03-Lubes and Car Care,
can only be assigned ONCE.
</a:Comment>
<a:ExtendedAttributesText>{77894B2F-5C8A-41A3-AAF2-C1D07AC2DAD1},BIM-core,138={20D43C80-304C-4F1F-937B-E4567B90A759},MappingLevel,3=BCM
{9A2CFDF7-6A96-42F8-B3A6-AF06089F9AB3},MapsToEntity,22=CUSTOMER_IN_SALES_AREA

</a:ExtendedAttributesText>
